# Generic Compose interpolation example for the delivered development instance.
#
# Copy this file to a local, uncommitted location (for example
# deployment/env.local) and export these values before running
# `docker compose up -d`, or pass them inline on the command line:
#
#   CONTROL_PLANE_IMAGE=control-plane:0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567 \
#   CONTROL_PLANE_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1 \
#   CONTROL_PLANE_PORT=8080 \
#   docker compose up -d
#
# Only these three inputs are interpolated. Application settings (database
# provider and path, production environment, container hosting switch, and the
# disabled Copilot agent) are set explicitly in compose.yaml, not here. This file
# is documentation only; it is never injected as a host environment file and is
# not read by Compose automatically.

# Required: an explicit, already-built image reference (tag or digest). Compose
# never builds or pulls this implicitly.
CONTROL_PLANE_IMAGE=control-plane:0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567

# Host interface for the published port. Defaults to loopback in compose.yaml.
CONTROL_PLANE_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1

# Host port mapped to the container HTTP port 8080. Defaults to 8080.
CONTROL_PLANE_PORT=8080
